SiliconForest, tip only: keep PDGOP buildable against the static string-matching IOKit.

Upstream f8715cf9 removed PDGOP.c's `#ifdef _PD_IOKITLIB_H` branch (PDIOKitLib's
string-based IOServiceMatching/IOServiceGetMatchingService) and left only the
CoreFoundation form, which needs IOKit.framework. The lab links PDGOP statically
with the string-based libIOKit.a into the compositor and the Mesa tests (no
CoreFoundation in those links). This restores the branch exactly as it was at
e7aa00a6; with IOKit.framework's header the CF form is still what compiles.

diff --git a/src/Libraries/PDGOP/PDGOP.c b/src/Libraries/PDGOP/PDGOP.c
